   "text": "I read the structure in four parts and combined them into one SMILES.\n\n1. **VHL-type ligand (right side).** It is a 4-hydroxyproline (hydroxyl on a hashed bond) whose carboxamide nitrogen carries an (S)-1-[4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl]ethyl group. I checked the methyl wedge on that benzylic carbon and found it to be S. The proline nitrogen is acylated by a tert-leucine residue (a tert-butyl group on the \u03b1-carbon). The \u03b1-carbon of that residue has a wedged NH.\n2. **Cyclobutane linker.** Both carbonyl substituents on the 1,3-disubstituted cyclobutane are drawn with wedges, so the ring is cis. One carbonyl is the amide to the tert-leucine NH. The other is an amide to a piperidine nitrogen.\n3. **Piperidine and central pyridine.** The piperidine is attached through its 4-position to the 4-position of a pyridine. That pyridine carries an NH-(4-cyanopyridin-2-yl) group at C2 and a 3,3-difluoropyrrolidin-1-yl group at C6.\n4. **Stereo assignment.** I did not look up the stereodescriptors for the proline and tert-leucine centres. I assumed the standard VHL-ligand configuration (the usual 2S,4R hydroxyproline and S tert-leucine) and wrote the SMILES parity to match. The benzylic carbon and the cis-cyclobutane were derived directly from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)CN1C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]2C[C@@H](C2)C(=O)N3CCC(CC3)c4cc(Nc5cc(C#N)ccn5)nc(c4)N6CCC(F)(F)C6)C(C)(C)C)c7ccc(cc7)-c8scnc8C"
